Here are some incredible trans female (and transfeminine) authors who deliver that same sharp, sarcastic, and funny literary voice. Their work spans genres from dark comedic fiction to brilliant, cynical cultural commentary:
## Darkly Funny & Cynical Fiction

* Torrey Peters
* The Voice: Incisive, deeply sarcastic, and fearlessly honest. She writes about modern queer and trans life with a brilliant, unsparing wit that deconstructs social norms and relationship dynamics.
   * Where to start: [Detransition, Baby](https://www.one worldlit.com), which is packed with sharp, dark humor, complex interpersonal drama, and hilariously biting commentary.
* Imogen Binnie
* The Voice: Deadpan, hyper-observant, and structurally chaotic. She is widely credited with helping pioneer modern trans fiction with a voice that feels like a conversation with your funniest, most cynical friend.
   * Where to start: [Nevada](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nevada), a cult classic punk-rock road trip novel featuring a deeply relatable, self-destructive, and sarcastic protagonist.
* Gretchen Felker-Martin
* The Voice: Visceral, pitch-black, and fiercely irreverent. She blends extreme horror with a deeply sharp, satirical edge that targets both mainstream society and online queer subcultures.
   * Where to start: [Cuckoo](https://cuckooamerica.com/) or [Manhunt](https://www.imdb.com/title/tt7801964/) (a brutal, darkly comedic sci-fi horror that is unapologetically unhinged).

## Sharp Satire & Brilliant Essays

* Casey Plett
* The Voice: Dry, empathetic but unsentimental, and quietly witty. Plett captures the mundane absurdities of daily life, dating, and community with a deeply realistic and often sarcastic charm.
   * Where to start: [A Dream of a Woman](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/57286652-a-dream-of-a-woman) or the novel [A Safe Girl to Love](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/22050397-a-safe-girl-to-love).
* Grace Lavery
* The Voice: Academic yet wildly camp, intellectual, and sharply humorous. She writes memoir and criticism with an incredibly distinct, playful, and irreverent high-brow energy.
   * Where to start: [Please Miss: A Heartbreaking Work of Staggering Penis](https://www.amazon.com/Please-Miss-Heartbreaking-Staggering-Penis/dp/1541620658), a genre-bending, hilarious, and surreal memoir.
* Fariha Róisín
* The Voice: While often writing serious cultural criticism, her fiction and essays carry a sharp, witty, and deeply observant edge regarding the absurdities of the modern wellness industry and cultural expectations.
   * Where to start: [Survival of the Thickest](https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/52764796-survival-of-the-thickest) (co-written with Michelle Buteau, highlighting sharp comedic pacing).

